# TDOC: the README's "Play clips together, and in order" section. One clip plays per role and
# the roles play together (a second launch on a role replaces the first). There is no chain:
# to play clips in order you launch them in LIVE and record a take, which replays the sequence.
# Shots: three roles playing together, and the take card.
wait 300
newsong 1
tap PLAY
# launch one clip on DRUMS, BASS and LEAD: they all play together
cursor 0 0
tap SEL
wait-bar 1
cursor 1 0
tap SEL
wait-bar 1
cursor 2 0
tap SEL
wait-bar 1
expect liveclip0 0
expect liveclip1 7
expect liveclip2 12
# a second launch on a role replaces the first, so a role never plays two clips at once
cursor 0 1
tap SEL
wait-bar 1
expect liveclip0 1

# --- LIVE, PADS: three roles playing at once ---
press PLAY
wait 700
release PLAY
wait 1400
expect mode 1
shot readme_together_live.png

# --- record a take that launches the clips in order, then replay it ---
tap REC
tapkey 0
wait 800
tapkey 7
wait 800
tapkey 12
wait 800
tap REC
wait-bar 2
expect takehas 1
# the take card lives in LIVE SETUP (EDIT, then the Take row)
tap EDIT
turn SELECT 6
tap SEL
wait 300
shot readme_together_take.png
tap SEL
wait 400
expect takeplaying 1
tap PLAY
wait 400
expect takeplaying 0
tap EDIT
wait 1400
press PLAY
wait 700
release PLAY
wait 1400
expect mode 0
dump readme_play_together.json
